      "extract": "[]{#sec:intro label=\"sec:intro\"} The classical Murnaghan--Nakayama rule provides an efficient recursive method to compute the values of irreducible characters of symmetric groups. This method can be adapted to the finite general linear and unitary groups, where it then allows to compute values of unipotent characters not on arbitrary but just on regular semisimple elements, see [@LM15 Prop. 3.3]. This adaptation",
